          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The field content of 11-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            contains a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+U%281%29-gauge+field"} higher U(1)-gauge field
            called the
            %em supergravity C-field
            or
            %em M-theory 3-form
            , which is locally a 3-form and globally
            %em some
            variant of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundle with connection
          %p
            There have been several suggestions for what
            %em precisely
            its correct global description must be, see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Models"} Models
            below
          %h2#ConsistencyConditions Consistency conditions
          %p
            Several subtle consistency conditions (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly+cancellation"}> quantum anomaly cancellation
            \-conditions) have been argued for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+quantization"} charge quantization
            of the supergravity C-field:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ShiftedCFieldFluxQuantizationCondition"} Shifted flux quantization condition
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#CFieldTadpoleCancellationCondition"} C-Field tadpole cancellation condition
          %h3#ShiftedCFieldFluxQuantizationCondition Shifted flux quantization condition
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization+condition"} shifted C-field flux quantization condition
            is a
            = succeed "-condition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+quantization"} charge quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            expected in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            class of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"}> field strength
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+4-form"} differential 4-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4 \in \Omega^4(X)
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            becomes integral after shifted by one quarter of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Pontryagin+class"} first Pontryagin class
          #eq:Shiftwed.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 4
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 4
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widetilde G_4
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  G_4 + \tfrac{1}{4}p_1(\nabla_{T X})
                  \\;\in\;
                  \\Omega^4(X)
          %p
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_{T X}
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+connection"} affine connection
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            to translate from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde G_4
            represents an
            = succeed "-class:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\widetilde G_4]
                  \\;\in\;
                  H^4(X, \mathbb{Z})
                  \\overset{H^4(X, \mathbb{Z}\hookrightarrow \mathbb{R})}{\longrightarrow}
                  H^4(X, \mathbb{R})
                  \\,.
          %p
            This condition was originally argued for in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96a"}> Witten 96a
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten96b"} Witten 96b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7d Chern-Simons theory
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is divisible by 2.
          %p
            Proposals for encoding this condition by a
            = succeed "-shifted" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wu+class"} Wu class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            were considered in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2C+and+M-Theory"} Hopkins-Singer 02
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DiaconescuFreedMoore03"} Diaconescu-Freed-Moore 03
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FSS12"} FSS 12
          %p
            It turns out that the shifted flux quantization condition on the C-field is naturally implied (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS1 19b, Prop. 4.12
            ) by the requirement that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            is the differential form datum underlying, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in unstable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            in degree 4 (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"}> Hypothesis H
            ).
          %h3#CFieldTadpoleCancellationCondition C-Field tadpole cancellation condition
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
            on 8-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(8)}
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole+cancellation+condition+for+the+supergravity+C-field"} tadpole cancellation condition for the supergravity C-field
            has been argued (
            %a{:href => "shifted+C-field+flux+quantization#SethiVafaWitten96"}> Sethi-Vafa-Witten 96
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "shifted+C-field+flux+quantization#BeckerBecker96"} Becker-Becker 96
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "shifted+C-field+flux+quantization#DasguptaMukhi97"} Dasgupta-Mukhi 97
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
