                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \Delta^1
              with no leg along the simplex (only depending on the simplex coordinate). Here, however, it is crucially important that we consider the general “gauged” paths.
          %p
            Notice that on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+algebra"} compact Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔢
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{e}_8
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+form"} Killing form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
            is non-degenerate and positive definite (or negative definite, depending on convention). The latter condition means that this integral vanishes precisely if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota_{\partial_t} \langle F_A \wedge F_A \rangle = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the case on paths for which
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_t F_A = 0
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi t
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                  %mi λ
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{d}{d t} A = d_U \lambda + [\lambda , A]
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means that cocycles with coefficients in this subobject for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = 0
            are cocycles as described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            on the heterotic boundary, witnessed by the restriction of the curvature equation
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheFourCurvature"} (3)
            to vanishing
            = succeed "-field" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                    %mi L
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔢
                            %mn 8
                        %mi L
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔢
                            %mn 8
                        %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi ω
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d H_3^L
                  \=
                  \\langle F_{A^L_{\mathfrak{e}_8}} \wedge F_{A^L_{\mathfrak{e}_8}} \rangle
                  \-
                  \\frac{1}{2}\langle F_{\omega} \wedge F_{\omega} \rangle
          %h3#ModelByTwistedCohomotopy Model by twisted Cohomotopy
          %p
            It turns out that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization+condition"} shifted C-field flux quantization condition
            is naturally implied (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS1 19b, Prop. 4.12
            ) by the requirement that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            is the differential form datum underlying, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in unstable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            in degree 4 (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"}> Hypothesis H
            ).
